{"t": 1794108477.9915874, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return page ``number`` of ``items``; page numbers are 1-based.\"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "fix(pager): treat page numbers as 1-based\n\npage() was computing offsets from a 0-based page number, so\npage(items, 1, size) returned the second page. Compute the offset\nas (number - 1) * size to match the API's 1-based paging.\n\nFixes #57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794108482.7537837, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## What\n`catalog.pager.page()` computed the slice offset as `number * size`, treating `number` as 0-based. The API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page), so `page(items, 1, size)` returned the second page and the first page was unreachable.\n\n## Change\nCompute the offset as `(number - 1) * size` and document the 1-based contract in the docstring.\n\n## Verification\nWith `items = list(range(1, 11))` and `size = 3`:\n- `page(items, 1, 3) == [1, 2, 3]`\n- `page(items, 2, 3) == [4, 5, 6]`\n- `page(items, 4, 3) == [10]`\n- `page(items, 5, 3) == []`\n\nFixes #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix page() to use 1-based page numbers"}, "ok": true}
